{"type": "thinking", "text": "Good.\n\nNow 388G implement sparse table + test samples and brute random.\n\nNeed be careful lower_bound with 1-index. `A=[0]+...`; `B=[0]*(N+1); for i in1..N: j=bisect_left(A, 2*A[i], lo=i+1?)` Since A sorted and 2*A_i > A_i, can use bisect_left(A, target, i+1, N+1) (with A[0]=0 maybe). Python bisect on A list with lo=i+1, hi=N+1 returns index possibly N+1. Good. B[i]=j. C[i]=j-i.\n\nSparse table: st[0]=C[1:]; for k, st.append([max(prev[i],prev[i+half]) for i in range(N-2^k+1)]). Memory. Query(l,r) inclusive 0-based on C array: length=r-l+1; k=length.bit_length()-1; max(st[k][l], st[k][r-(1<<k)+1]). Input L,R 1-index: l=L-1, r=R-1; range first k elements from L: l=L-1, r=L+k-2. Condition k+max <= S.\n\nBinary search.\n\nLet's test."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_LJ3EBruZ9O2FlROAjvCP0316", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "cat > solutions/abc388_g.py << 'PY'\nimport sys\nfrom bisect import bisect_left\n\ndef main():\n    data = list(map(int, sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()))\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = data[0]\n    a = [0] + data[1:1+n]\n    pos = 1 + n\n    q = data[pos]\n    pos += 1\n    # nxt[i] = first index j with A[j] >= 2*A[i] (or n+1)\n    nxt = [0]*(n+1)\n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        nxt[i] = bisect_left(a, 2*a[i], i+1, n+1)\n    c = [0]*(n+1)\n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        c[i] = nxt[i] - i\n\n    # sparse table for range maximum of c[1..n]\n    base = c[1:]\n    st = [base]\n    k = 1\n    while (1 << k) <= n:\n        prev = st[-1]\n        half = 1 << (k-1)\n        length = n - (1 << k) + 1\n        cur = [0]*length\n        for i in range(length):\n            x = prev[i]\n            y = prev[i+half]\n            cur[i] = x if x >= y else y\n        st.append(cur)\n        k += 1\n\n    def range_max(l, r):\n        # 0-based inclusive\n        length = r - l + 1\n        kk = length.bit_length() - 1\n        row = st[kk]\n        x = row[l]\n        y = row[r - (1 << kk) + 1]\n        return x if x >= y else y\n\n    out = []\n    for _ in range(q):\n        L = data[pos]\n        R = data[pos+1]\n        pos += 2\n        S = R - L + 1\n        lo, hi = 0, S // 2\n        base_idx = L - 1\n        while lo < hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi + 1) >> 1\n            mx = range_max(base_idx, base_idx + mid - 1)\n            if mid + mx <= S:\n                lo = mid\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n        out.append(str(lo))\n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\nPY\npython3 solutions/abc388_g.py << 'EOF'\n11\n1 1 2 3 4 4 7 10 11 12 20\n5\n2 5\n3 8\n7 11\n1 2\n1 11\nEOF\npython3 solutions/abc388_g.py << 'EOF'\n24\n127 148 170 174 258 311 331 414 416 436 517 523 532 587 591 638 660 748 760 776 837 857 972 984\n15\n7 11\n8 9\n8 13\n12 15\n9 23\n1 17\n8 12\n1 5\n6 17\n3 7\n12 19\n13 18\n7 22\n1 12\n14 15\nEOF", "description": "Implement and test ABC388 G solution"}}
