{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now G. Need implement and verify samples. Let's formalize DP.\n\nWe'll use basis (1+x)^D. Need careful with layer S0 and final edge count.\n\nInitialize dp dictionary mapping (s,a,ec,p) -> packed big int polynomial in D. Actually we process levels s increasing. We can maintain dict for current s? Transitions from states at s to larger s. Since s increases, we can use `states` dict keyed (s,a,ec,p) and process s from1 to N-1. Easier: array of dicts per s: `dp[s] = dict (a,ec,p)->packed`. Initialize dp[1][(1,1,0)] = 1 (polynomial D=0 coefficient1). Then for s from1 to N-1, for each state, transitions b=1..N-s; if new_s<=N. Add to dp[new_s]. But new_s > s so when processing s, all incoming to s already done because transitions only from smaller s. We can reduce packed digits for dp[s] states before use. We can do reduction when iterating dp[s]. This avoids storing unreduced across levels. Need ensure dp[s] packed coefficients haven't overflowed base before reduction. Accumulation into state at s comes from multiple previous levels s-b and states; each contribution coefficient < old coeff (<P after reductions of previous levels) * c where c mod P (<P) => <P^2 ~1e18 <2^60. Number of contributions to a fixed (s,a,ec,p) from previous levels: b = s - s_prev, for each b there is unique s_prev. For each b, previous states with various a_prev, ec_prev, p_prev. Number a_prev up to s_prev, ec maybe, p 2. But ec_new fixed and p_new fixed; p_prev determined, ec_prev determined by ec_new and whether new layer even. So only a_prev varies (~s). Also j varies b+1. Total contributions ~Σ_b s_prev*(b+1) <= N * Σ_b b ~30*465=13950. <2^14. Coefficient sum <2^14 * 2^60 =2^74. K=96 safe. Even if c not reduced? c = C(N-s,b)*C(b,j) mod P <P. Good.\n\nBut old packed polynomial coefficients are reduced mod P (<P). We reduce every dp[s] before transitions. Need also exact no carries during accumulation. Bound safe.\n\nNow transition generation:\nFor state (s,a,ec,p) with packed poly P_old (digits coeff[D]).\nFor each b in 1..N-s:\n  label = comb(N-s, b) mod P.\n  new_p = 1-p\n  new_ec = ec + (b if new_p==0 else 0)\n  if new_ec > N//2? We only care final ec=N/2; ec nondecreasing, so can prune if new_ec > N/2. Also potential odd count? We can prune if number odd vertices >N/2 too? Odd count = s - ec. For new state, if (new_s - new_ec) > N/2, prune. This helps.\n  D2 = b*(b-1)//2  # within\n  for j in 0..b:\n    inc = D2 + a*(b-j)\n    coeff = label * C(b,j) with sign (-1)^j mod P\n    term = (P_old << (K*inc)) * coeff  (P_old digits coefficients; multiplication by coeff <P)\n    add to dp[new_s][(b,new_ec,new_p)] packed integer.\nBut multiplication `P_old * coeff` and shift. Since P_old is packed coeff base B=2^K. Multiplying by coeff (<P<2^30) does not cause carries across digits if each digit*coeff < B? Digit <P, coeff <P => <P^2<2^60 <2^96, so no carries. Good. Then shift by K*inc bits. Add.\n\nCould combine label into coeff. Compute binomial C(b,j) and sign. Since b<=30, precompute comb_small[b][j] mod P? They are small integers <=C(30,15)=155117520 <P? P can be as low as1e8, which is less than155M, so need mod P. Compute global comb table up to maxN (30) mod P using Pascal. Then label=C(N-s,b) via comb[N-s][b] mod P. Good.\n\nAt final s=N, we only need states with ec=N/2. But transitions to N may include new_ec exactly N/2; prune others. Note p irrelevant. We sum packed polynomials from dp[N][(a,N/2,p)] for all a,p. But dp[N] coefficients may be unreduced if we didn't process s=N. Need reduce or sum then reduce. Summing packed big ints: coefficients each <P but accumulated from transitions with bound <2^96, so final dp[N] digits <2^96. We can add all final packed ints (at most ~30*2) safely (<2^96) then unpack/reduce into total_coeff[D] mod P. Alternatively reduce each then sum.\n\nThen compute ans[M] for M from N-1 to maxE=N*(N-1)//2:\n ans[M] = Σ_{D=0}^{maxE} total_coeff[D] * C(D,M) mod P.\nNote D might start at? Could be